# Taller Cloth Awning and Deeper Scalloped Hem

Status: DONE
Milestone: M28 Longer roof proportions with aligned fabric motion
Dependencies: 26_FABRIC_AWNING_AND_SCALLOP_SEAM.todo; 32_CONTINUOUS_WOOD_AND_RAISED_SIGN.todo

## Purpose

The owner wants the whole cloth roof taller and its bottom curved hanging portion
longer. Preserve its width, cream/blush palette, wooden sign and interactive fabric.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve current SVG, motion model, CSS, tests, docs and context.
- [x] Increase both page and entrance roof heights by50%.
- [x] Extend the original24scallops from sourceY174to234on a240pxartboard.
- [x] Lengthen both the hanging stems and curved ends, without clipping the hem.
- [x] Expand the cloth mesh from15to17rows and retain exact rail/side anchors.
- [x] Keep rigid rail paint native while the cloth mesh animates.
- [x] Check actual lower-hem pixels,50%height ratio, pinning and responsive entry fitting.
- [x] Finish site/entry checks and refresh affected launch images/portrait variants.
- [x] Publish only the scoped roof/motion/artwork update.

## Acceptance criteria

- Full-width page roof120-270pxtall instead of80-180px.
- Source hanging region128-234 instead of128-174; curved end181-234instead of151-174.
- No stale180pxmotion coordinates, clipped scallops or moving rigid rails.
- Pointer/scroll response, exactrest, reducedmotion, fallbacks and scene controls remain.
- No source-photo changes, localcream changes or additional image-tool views.

